      "output": {
        "decision": "answer",
        "reason": "The evidence (Language Models section) fully describes how language models are used to predict/rank humorous statements: Ngram models trained on two corpora (funny tweets from @midnight and news data) assign a probability to each tweet; tweets with higher probability under the funny-tweet model are considered funnier, while tweets with lower probability under the news model are considered funnier; bigrams and trigrams were used as features, with KenLM, modified Kneser-Ney smoothing and back-off. This directly and completely answers the question."
      },
